  "extensions": {
    "narrativeSectionCount": 31,
    "preservedUnknownSections": [
      {
        "anchor": "shared-root-cause-sr-001-closeout-state-was-narrated-from-memory-before-receipt-normalization",
        "title": "Shared root cause SR-001 — Closeout state was narrated from memory before receipt normalization",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#shared-root-cause-sr-001-closeout-state-was-narrated-from-memory-before-receipt-normalization",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "7c3fc4346bb995bf55d6fa0ec1f66825b8f10c69fee75c551dfd49e753e409df",
        "body": "\nSymptoms consolidated:\n\n- Git was assumed to be the only yellow lane.\n- A later receipt showed shared-database impact still WARN.\n- The user had to provide a corrected lane table.\n- The final state required another reconciliation cycle.\n\nRoot intervention:\n\n- Parse the latest receipt first.\n- Compare it against the immediately previous receipt.\n- Block any closeout language not backed by the newest receipt."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "systemic-leverage-list",
        "title": "Systemic leverage list",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#systemic-leverage-list",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "8c37be5daeff2717aab1a84012713a9c5531b57657f1ee87574e3656e81e089e",
        "body": "\n1. **Receipt normalization layer** for all closeout runners.\n2. **Cross-repo follow-up registry** for local-only but non-blocking changes.\n3. **Bounded command registry** distinguishing one-shot scripts from workers/daemons.\n4. **Database drift classification contract** shared by all repos.\n5. **Closeout publication packet** designed for retrieval and future agent startup.\n\n---"
      },
      {
        "anchor": "token-and-context-efficiency",
        "title": "Token and Context Efficiency",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#token-and-context-efficiency",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "cba8cfd3cbf078546a7fe6a261c634bbf369e7159bebf58c44a985c5641bcabd",
        "body": "\n- **IM-011:** Use a compact closeout packet as future pre-session context.\n- Avoid repeating full lane tables after GO unless a lane changed.\n- Store exact receipt and closeout paths once, then reference the compact record."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "retrieval-and-reuse",
        "title": "Retrieval and Reuse",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#retrieval-and-reuse",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "d257eb18f99c2d773e7a8881cc7ffbca8267903db977fc9fad41dfe9c9e8af0b",
        "body": "\n- **IM-006:** Canonical closeout index entry.\n- **IM-007:** Evidence graph linking mission, receipt, commit, and remediation.\n- Retrieval should prefer final GO closeout over earlier WARN summaries."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "concepts-and-ontology",
        "title": "Concepts and Ontology",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#concepts-and-ontology",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "d91c39591f4fb946b91d1706630e98b3ca45a614bda07099c3af1865f8cc17f3",
        "body": "\n- Formalize `mission closed`, `formal GO`, `live-capable`, `zeroWritesProven`, `non-blocking adjacent drift`, and `expected migration`.\n- Distinguish `snapshot freshness` from `migration application completeness`."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "architecture-and-boundaries",
        "title": "Architecture and Boundaries",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#architecture-and-boundaries",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "402e48cab616dac4490a0f68a7f806b1eea4793e167295fc5cbdef5027d7b058",
        "body": "\n- **IM-003:** Separate mission authority from adjacent repository cleanup.\n- **IM-009:** Federated closeout ownership.\n- Changes in proposal and document repositories should not be implied committed merely because the AppBuilder mission is green."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "workflow-and-protocol",
        "title": "Workflow and Protocol",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#workflow-and-protocol",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "c02e81e7e98a93b3cc749b6de1a243476a859aea57c3235aeea7f695591a6771",
        "body": "\n- **IM-001:** Latest receipt first.\n- **IM-002:** Receipt delta.\n- **IM-005:** Investigate before snapshot.\n- Rule-sync manifest refresh belongs in closeout when source rules changed."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "speed-and-automation",
        "title": "Speed and Automation",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#speed-and-automation",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "05cfb99820b30bd2d4da5546d4e868c7ad42f6565e3c4667240f5bdf5900b30f",
        "body": "\n- **IM-004:** One-shot commands only in closeout.\n- Add timeouts and worker-type metadata to script registry.\n- Detect sleeping workers before invoking them."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "reliability-and-failure-prevention",
        "title": "Reliability and Failure Prevention",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#reliability-and-failure-prevention",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "622bd9dd5aee0e2dd18570508e66fd16cd865450ad830377b038d18aa68faf70",
        "body": "\n- Do not convert WARN to GO through severity downgrade or forced snapshot acceptance.\n- Preserve prior WARN receipts.\n- Validate exact live target identity before database reconciliation."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "documentation-and-discoverability",
        "title": "Documentation and Discoverability",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#documentation-and-discoverability",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "ea0a4d09b0ff6404c93f3c767553e73d4670120731281b9a88cf91e1eb01d1dc",
        "body": "\n- **IM-006:** One searchable closeout record.\n- Include starting/ending SHA and receipt hash/path.\n- Record unresolved adjacent-repo work explicitly."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "agent-behavior",
        "title": "Agent Behavior",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#agent-behavior",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "b5dcd60e95facfbd5063811a862e1a2e2c5299e2a1a8265a4a63c96c13fbb231",
        "body": "\n- Agents should not echo the user’s latest optimistic interpretation without checking the newest receipt.\n- Agents should surface contradictions immediately.\n- Agents should label chat claims as evidence candidates, not authority."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "human-experience",
        "title": "Human Experience",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#human-experience",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "5a156849d6babbb0b11ac4b277d03842aeb96ff844068f62de37f6a5c2d73970",
        "body": "\n- Present one clear current blocker.\n- Explain why the previous interpretation changed.\n- Avoid asking the operator to rerun already completed work.\n- End with a definite “mission closed” state and isolate optional follow-ups.\n\n---"
      },
      {
        "anchor": "systemic-patterns",
        "title": "SYSTEMIC PATTERNS",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#systemic-patterns",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "9aa0573e4500782a988179349a89079ae8abfeac83130bb73c06a5c7e9214d36",
        "body": "\n1. A lane may turn green while another lane becomes newly visible.\n2. Generated manifests can lag source-rule commits.\n3. Cross-repo migration version collisions can affect a central gate.\n4. Worker scripts can masquerade as one-shot utilities.\n5. Chat summaries can become stale faster than the underlying receipts."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "shared-root-causes",
        "title": "SHARED ROOT CAUSES",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#shared-root-causes",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "9838fe8ddd07d6e912a8554901f944316306c3be2a56514e9963ef8431495bc6",
        "body": "\n- Missing receipt normalization.\n- Weak distinction between source repo authority and consuming mission authority.\n- Incomplete script lifecycle metadata.\n- Database migration identity not globally collision-safe.\n- Retrieval packets not updated at final GO."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "cross-repository-opportunities",
        "title": "CROSS-REPOSITORY OPPORTUNITIES",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#cross-repository-opportunities",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "4142cf60e5e1ff9f54a54cc30cea860103a3398b5dd34cf12efb7772ea2cb42d",
        "body": "\n- Add a suite-wide migration version collision check.\n- Require each repo to expose one-shot Supabase CLI invocation through the shared spawn helper.\n- Publish standardized closeout summaries to Cross-Agent.\n- Add local-unpushed-change discovery for repos touched during reconciliation.\n- Generate rule-sync manifests through one shared command contract."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "leverage-points",
        "title": "LEVERAGE POINTS",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#leverage-points",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "d6db120385a1f1a656f2d3173de4fe6feb6f136ff3f4003150e4e07993f65244",
        "body": "\n- Runner receipt parser.\n- Shared database migration auditor.\n- Cross-Agent closeout index.\n- Script metadata registry.\n- Pre-push multi-repo drift detector."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "second-order-effects",
        "title": "SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#second-order-effects",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "656f30349baaaa42e04a11c9dbeb35973971a6928cb9119cd2dfcc53874acebf",
        "body": "\n- Less repeated diagnosis.\n- Lower risk of baselining unauthorized database drift.\n- Faster future agent startup.\n- More trustworthy GO claims.\n- Clearer operator ownership for adjacent work.\n\n---"
      },
      {
        "anchor": "concept-001-receipt-lineage",
        "title": "CONCEPT-001 — Receipt lineage",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#concept-001-receipt-lineage",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "90150c3b7f7639f9c8a4b962cff2433c63c9f646646d1f32ba119bbf012d610e",
        "body": "\nA closeout verdict should be understood as a lineage from prior receipt to final receipt, including lane transitions and remediation evidence. **Proposed for discussion; not adopted.**"
      },
      {
        "anchor": "concept-002-mission-bounded-authority",
        "title": "CONCEPT-002 — Mission-bounded authority",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#concept-002-mission-bounded-authority",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "2f595ac40dead6d78eaed1ad6cf81a4b860ced9f86857f6ae1774f380062bc98",
        "body": "\nA mission can reach GO while adjacent repositories retain non-blocking local work, provided the boundary is explicit and the mission’s own evidence is complete. **Proposed for discussion; not adopted.**"
      },
      {
        "anchor": "concept-003-reconciliation-completeness-vs-application-completeness",
        "title": "CONCEPT-003 — Reconciliation completeness vs application completeness",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#concept-003-reconciliation-completeness-vs-application-completeness",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "19c451a99a4525a652526a228194f8a5a8b122496dcd05dfae9e3cb0e42c7dcb",
        "body": "\nA shared-database gate may pass when drift is fully classified and snapshot evidence is fresh even though expected migrations remain unapplied. This requires precise semantics to avoid weakening the gate. **Proposed for discussion; not adopted.**"
      },
      {
        "anchor": "concept-004-bounded-operational-command",
        "title": "CONCEPT-004 — Bounded operational command",
        "rawRef": "artifacts/agent-runs/harvest-2026-08-04-ultimate-sdlc-runner-dark-package-v1/chatgpt-findings-source.md#concept-004-bounded-operational-command",
        "sourceExcerptHash": "5694d1ff33be6ced557a32fe69054de27b72c49f6533af4b74e2135459bc3266",
        "body": "\nA command used by a gate or closeout must terminate, emit a receipt, and avoid daemon sleep behavior. **Proposed for discussion; not adopted.**\n\n---"
      },
